#{[17592186433682 #edb/ref 1080 "(R-{A}^{T}A)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433682 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433682 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8091e143-1c62-5487-9984-834771a83882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433683 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6bf75937-c3db-5f40-8e20-ee3efbdf6a43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139766" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,x={Q}^{T}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the matrix equation above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "553d1e63-f638-55c5-a882-d8b6a7339c64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433684 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ R\\,\\,x & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is $R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440834 #edb/ref 1080 "$A$ and $b$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440834 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440834 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29c6894b-ca73-55e4-b9e5-4515a24ac505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440835 #edb/ref 1080 "$m\\cdot {Q}^{-1}$ and $b$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440835 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440835 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b99f2e8-4b05-5e94-b564-250f2853615a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440836 #edb/ref 1080 "$b$ and $Q$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440836 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440836 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4dd231d7-89bb-5f54-b089-0db260de5eac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440837 #edb/ref 1080 "${Q}^{T}$ and $b$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440837 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440837 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eef0bb49-3a2a-51f2-9a63-905441460146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440838 #edb/ref 1080 "$Q$ and $b$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440838 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440838 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "efe2b6b7-9514-56b9-905d-32ae3b168ebe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440839 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "75513403-98f8-5580-8da1-119fb356a265" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440840 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440840 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139751" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440840 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440840 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nx={R}^{-1}\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440840 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5d70a3f-a448-5de5-8896-cf994f65054e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440840 #edb/ref 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,\\bbox[6px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{|}{Q}^{T}\\,\\,}\\,\\,\\bbox[6px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{|}b\\phantom{|}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${Q}^{T}$ and $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
